\title{RSFactor: Wrapper for R's Factor Scalar Values}
\description{
\code{RSFactor} is a subclass of \code{RSString} designed to wrap R factor values while preserving
their level definitions and ordering information. This enables safe scalar-level comparison
and hashing while retaining the semantics of categorical variables.

During initialization, the factor is converted to a character string for value storage,
while \code{levels()} and \code{ordered()} provide access to the original factor metadata.
}
\section{Methods}{

\itemize{
\item \code{asFactor()} – Reconstructs the original factor with levels and ordering
\item \code{levels()} – Returns the vector of factor levels
\item \code{ordered()} – Returns TRUE if the factor was ordered
\item \code{compare(other, na.last = TRUE)} – Compares factor values respecting ordering
}
}

\section{Usage}{

Use \code{RSFactor_withFactor(val)} to construct safely from a factor value.
}

\examples{
f <- factor("low", levels = c("low", "medium", "high"), ordered = TRUE)
obj <- RSFactor_withFactor(f)
obj$levels()      # "low" "medium" "high"
obj$ordered()     # TRUE
obj$asFactor()    # reconstructs original factor

}
